        4.18.3 How to read Core syntax (from some -ddump flags)

GHC IRs:
    Parsed
    Renamed - names/scopes resolved, unique identifiers
    Typechecked
    Core - System F
    STG - Spineless tagless G-machine, low-level functional exposing laziness, closures
    Cmm - low-level imperative IR, interface to LLVM/native

Access typechecked: GHC API’s TypecheckedModule, GHC typechecker dumps


4.18.1 Dumping out compiler intermediate structures
-ddump-pass Make a debugging dump after pass <pass> (may be common enough to need a short form. . . ). You can get
all of these at once (lots of output) by using -v5, or most of them with -v4. Some of the most useful ones are:
-ddump-rn: renamer output
-ddump-tc: typechecker output
-ddump-splices: Dump Template Haskell expressions that we splice in, and what Haskell code the expression
evaluates to.
-ddump-types: Dump a type signature for each value defined at the top level of the module. The list is sorted
alphabetically. Using -dppr-debug dumps a type signature for all the imported and system-defined things as well;
useful for debugging the compiler.
-ddump-deriv: derived instances
-ddump-ds: desugarer output
-ddump-spec: output of specialisation pass
-ddump-rules: dumps all rewrite rules specified in this module; see Section 7.14.6.
-ddump-simpl: simplifier output (Core-to-Core passes)
-ddump-prep: output of core preparation pass
-ddump-flatC: flattened Abstract C
-ddump-tc-trace Make the type checker be *real* chatty about what it is upto.

GHC API: internal compiler shipped with each release - parse, typecheck, Core, parts of pipeline, plugins, compile code dynamically. unstable, highly coupled to installed version, platform-specific dependencies
ghc-lib: decoupled, non-compiling library for API - use front-end (parse, rename, typecheck) without dependencies on specific version. no code-generation
    used for tools like linter, lsp, static tools
    includes generating TcEvBinds - evidence bindings, HsTypechecked, CoreExpr
        explicit dictionary bindings, coercion evidence, EvVar and EvTerm structure, ModGuts (Core + binds + rules) after desugaring
        coercion evidence includes solved equality constraints like a~Bool recorded as EvTerms
        type class dicts store evidence for type equalities, functional dependencies
        EvVar is a variable whose type is an evidence type, like dictionary for class constraint. constraint solver binds EvVar to EvTerm. EvTerm constructs or provides evidence. dictionary construction - evidence for class with methods based on superclasses. dictionary selection - extract superclass dictionary from class constraint. coercion - witness for type equality.
Using ghc-lib you can:
Run the parser → HsParsedModule
Run the renamer → HsRenamed
Run the typechecker → TcGblEnv, containing evidence bindings
    TcGblEnv has all typechecker info for current module, equiv ModGuts but before desugar
    central state threaded thru.
    Typechecked declarations in Haskell syntax (not Core)
    type, class, instance decls
    evidence bindings
    top-level identifiers w types
    fields of TcGblEnv:
        tcg_binds :: LHsBinds GhcTc  - Every top-level binding, typechecked, but still in Tc syntax.
        tcg_tcs :: [TyCon]
        tcg_insts :: [InstInfo]
        tcg_fam_insts :: [FamInst]
        tcg_exports, tcg_imports
        ^ all type decls, class insts, families defined in module
        tcg_ev_binds :: Bag EvBind
        tcg_ev_binds_var :: EvVar -- the top-level evidence binder
        ^ evidence produced by typechecking: dicts, coercions, equality proofs
        global reader environment - names and scopes for identifiers
    typechecked AST, HsSyn GhcTc is desugared, rewritten, expanded, and normalized in many places:
Do-notation is rewritten into binds.
List comprehensions are transformed.
Pattern matches become case trees.
Type applications are inserted.
Implicit arguments and dictionaries are added.
Rebindable syntax is resolved.
Operator fixities may not match original grouping.
Layout information (indentation) is lost.
Original parentheses are gone
Run the desugarer → ModGuts, containing dictionaries as CoreExprs

Prettyprint typechecked program: 
pprLHsBinds tcg_binds
ppr (tcg_binds :: LHsBinds GhcTc)
Haskell-like, desugars to explicit >>=, contains typechecker artifacts like wrappers and evidence passing


Evidence binding:
f :: Eq a => a -> a -> Bool
f x y = x == y
Typechecker introduces a dictionary variable for the Eq a constraint (ev_eq_a :: Eq a).
The function is represented as:
f = \ev_eq_a x y -> eq# ev_eq_a x y
ev_eq_a is the EvVar (the binder for the evidence)
It is passed explicitly as a function argument
This is “evidence passing”


